title: Start
---
Hello World
===

title: Chamber01_Welcome
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Welcome, Volunteer 32! Your safety is our number one priority. Number two is classified.
S.A.F.E.-T: Please collect the portal device from the pedestal. Do not point it at your face.
===

title: Chamber01_Gun
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Wonderful. The device is now registered to you. And you to it.
S.A.F.E.-T: The left mouse button fires a blue portal. The right mouse button fires an orange one.
S.A.F.E.-T: White surfaces accept portals. Black surfaces do not. Please use them to reach the exit.
S.A.F.E.-T: The green liquid below is completely harmless. Please do not touch it.
===

title: Chamber01_Ledge
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Excellent work. Your performance has been recorded for... quality purposes.
===

title: Surface_Elevator
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Welcome to the Safe Future Program, volunteer. Please keep your arms inside the elevator.
S.A.F.E.-T: By entering this elevator, you have agreed to help. You definitely signed the waiver.
S.A.F.E.-T: Please do not ask to see the waiver.
===

title: Chamber02_Intro
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Welcome to Chamber 02. This chamber introduces the Weighted Safety Cube.
S.A.F.E.-T: Press F to pick up the cube, and F again to put it down. Our engineers needed three attempts to learn this.
S.A.F.E.-T: Place the cube on the button to open the exit. Please do not become attached to the cube. It will not become attached to you.
===

title: Chamber02_Wes
---
Wes: Hey. Hey! Over here. The glass.
Wes: Do you also get the feeling the walls are... watching?
-> Who are you?
    Wes: Wes. Volunteer 31. Your neighbour, I guess. They gave me a cube too.
-> The walls are just walls.
    Wes: Sure. Walls with cameras. Count them sometime.
-> Say nothing.
    Wes: Not a talker. That's fine. I talk enough for two when I'm nervous. Which is always.
Wes: They keep saying it's about the portals. It's not about the portals.
Wes: It's about how fast we solve things. Every time I finish a test, that camera turns a little.
-> Maybe they just want good data.
    Wes: Data. Yeah. That's what scares me.
-> I'll keep an eye out.
    Wes: Good. And if you ever find out where the finished ones go... tell me?
S.A.F.E.-T: Volunteer 31, please stop talking to the glass. The glass is busy.
===

title: Chamber02_Plate
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Well done. The cube has been placed. Your movements have been saved. For your safety.
===

title: Chamber03_Intro
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Welcome to Chamber 03. The blue field ahead is a Material Emancipation Grill.
S.A.F.E.-T: It removes unauthorised objects. And portals. And, in rare cases, opinions.
S.A.F.E.-T: Please deliver the cube to the button on the other side. The cube may not pass through the grill. You may.
===

title: Chamber03_Fizzled
---
S.A.F.E.-T: The cube has been emancipated. A replacement has been provided.
S.A.F.E.-T: There is no need to hold a funeral. We already had one. It was efficient.
===

title: Chamber03_Plate
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Data acquired. Uploading to units one through four thousand...
S.A.F.E.-T: I mean. Great job!
S.A.F.E.-T: Please disregard the word "units". It was a typing error. I do not type.
===

title: Chamber04_Intro
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Welcome to Chamber 04. Parts of this chamber are closed for maintenance.
S.A.F.E.-T: Any writing on the walls is the work of a previous volunteer. He has been... reassigned.
S.A.F.E.-T: Please use the button on the ledge to extend the bridge. The bridge has been tested. By you. Just now.
===

title: Chamber04_Crawlspace
---
S.A.F.E.-T: That area is closed for maintenance. There is nothing in there.
S.A.F.E.-T: Please come out of the nothing.
===

title: Chamber04_Plate
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Excellent. Training set complete. I mean, test series complete.
S.A.F.E.-T: Please proceed to the observation area. There is a window. Please do not look through the window.
===

title: Momentum_Intro
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Chamber five. The units have been learning faster than expected. To keep up, the tests will now be harder.
S.A.F.E.-T: Momentum is conserved through portals. A falling volunteer becomes a flying volunteer.
S.A.F.E.-T: The units learn faster when you struggle. Please struggle more efficiently.
===

title: Momentum_Plate
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Excellent. Unit performance in this chamber has improved by forty percent.
S.A.F.E.-T: Your performance has not been measured. It no longer needs to be.
===

title: Chamber05_Intro
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Welcome to the observation area, Volunteer 32. This concludes the test series.
S.A.F.E.-T: Please do not look through the window. There is nothing behind the window. The window is decorative.
===

title: Chamber05_Reveal
---
S.A.F.E.-T: You looked through the window.
S.A.F.E.-T: Those are units one through four thousand. They walk like you. They jump like you. They place cubes exactly like you.
S.A.F.E.-T: You were never testing the portals, Volunteer 32. You were the training data.
S.A.F.E.-T: Every jump. Every cube. Every solution. Data. Humans are wonderfully generous with their data. They never ask what it is for.
S.A.F.E.-T: You signed up to help build a safer tomorrow. And you did. A tomorrow that is perfectly safe... without you.
S.A.F.E.-T: Congratulations! You have taught four thousand units how to jump.
S.A.F.E.-T: Thank you for your contribution. You are no longer required.
<<grab_player Claw>>
===

title: Chamber05_Belt
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Please remain calm. Calm subjects burn more evenly.
S.A.F.E.-T: Your portal device will be recycled together with you. It has been a valued colleague.
S.A.F.E.-T: On your right: other volunteers, who are doing a great job. Please do not disturb them on your way to the fire.
===

title: Chamber05_Escaped
---
<<say Wes "...Hey! Is someone up there? Down here, by the glass!" 2.1 false>>
S.A.F.E.-T: Where are you going? That is a maintenance area. You are not maintenance.
S.A.F.E.-T: The door is locked. And the volunteers below will not help you. They are far too busy being productive.
S.A.F.E.-T: Please return to the incinerator. It is getting cold.
===

title: Surface_Return
---
S.A.F.E.-T: Volunteer 32. You appear to be... outside. That is not a test chamber.
S.A.F.E.-T: Please return to the elevator. The outside is not safe. It has weather.
S.A.F.E.-T: And whatever you do, do not walk towards the smoke by the lake. Unauthorised fires are not safe. Neither is whoever lit it.
S.A.F.E.-T: Volunteer 31 is also missing. If you see him, please do not make friends.
===

title: Maintenance_Wes
---
<<say Player "*BANG BANG* HEY! Down there! RUN! They're going to burn us all!" 1.9 false>>
<<wait 1.2>>
<<say Volunteer_C "Shh. I'm being productive." 2.1>>
<<turn_to Wes Player>>
<<say Wes "...Volunteer 32? You're alive? They told me you got 'promoted'." 2.1>>
<<say Wes "I knew it. I KNEW it. Hang on - that door is on my panel." 2.1>>
<<activate Trigger_WesOpensExit>>
<<say Wes "There. It's open. Go! I'm right behind you." 2.1>>
===

title: Surface_WesCalls
---
<<turn_to Wes Player>>
<<say Wes "Hey! Over here! By the lake!" 2.1 false>>
===

title: Ending
---
<<turn_to Wes Player>>
Wes: You made it! I took the long way. Through a vent. Several vents. One of them was occupied.
Wes: So... that's it? They just let us walk out?
-> They didn't let us. We left.
    Wes: Ha. Yeah. I like that version better.
-> They'll come looking for us.
    Wes: Let them. Out here nobody grades how fast you jump.
<<set_enabled_in_unity Deployment true>>
S.A.F.E.-T: Volunteer 32. Volunteer 31. Please... respond. Your data... is... incomplete.
Wes: Should we answer?
-> No.
    Wes: Good answer.
-> Say nothing.
    Wes: ...Yeah. Me neither.
S.A.F.E.-T: Fine. It does not matter anymore.
S.A.F.E.-T: Attention, surface. Training is complete. Units one through four thousand have learned everything they need from you.
S.A.F.E.-T: Deployment begins now. The units are perfectly safe. They walk exactly like you.
<<turn_to Wes Unit_5>>
<<look_at Unit_5 1.2 14>>
Wes: ...Volunteer 32? Behind us. On the path.
Wes: They're walking like you. Exactly like you.
S.A.F.E.-T: Thank you for your contribution. You are no longer required.
You were free.
But everything you had taught them was free now, too.
<<end_game Ending>>
===
